  "details": "Japanese, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese Hanji (Kanji) have the same character code but look different.\n\n\"刃直海角骨入\" is a good example. When this string is displayed in Japanese, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese fonts respectively, they look the same, but the position of the parts and the number of strokes are different.\n\nCurrently, the Chinese characters used in VRChat are Japanese Hanji, but to someone using Simplified Chinese or Traditional Chinese Hanji, it looks strange.\n\nRefer to the attached image, Switch between the main Hanji characters used depending on the language you have set up.\n\nComparison of Hanji in different languages:\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_unification#Examples_of_language-dependent_glyphs",
